{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1125716-reworking-rage-use-and-frenzy","id":1125716,"title":"Reworking Rage Use and Frenzy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-06T15:58:45-07:00","id":1125716,"title":"Reworking Rage Use and Frenzy","content":"Hello all,<br /> <br /> After reading the Vampire 4th edition rules, came in mind an idea how to make Rage more appealing and frenzy more dangerous, since there have been mentions that frenzy is not a serious or often danger in Werewolf 20 game sessions.<br /> So the idea is to reverse the Rage expediture, which means that instead of burning rage and remove them from the pool, to mark the Rage boxes you use every turn and keep them marked, the next turn you keep marking rage until you gather enough to roll for frenzy.<br /> <br /> This use will make Rage more powerful but more dangerous at the same time, why? Lets see an example.<br /> <br /> A Ragabash with Rage 1 finds himself in a dangerous situation and uses his Rage for 3 turns in order to finish fast with the issue, he can spend only 1 Rage per turn, so at the beginning of the third turn he will have 3 marked boxes and at the fourth turn he will have 4 Rage boxes marked, since Rage can go above permanent rating, but oops he has only Willpower of 3 so he rolls 4 dice at the proper moon phase (and crinos form) difficulty. Each success removes one temporary Rage from the boxes, so if the ragabash of the example brings 2 successes and will not enter frenzy, he will erase 2 boxes, if he gets 4 successes he will mark off all his temporary Rage and enter frenzy. If the Ragabash gets no successes his rage may go up to 5 the next time and frenzy will become more dangerous.<br /> <br /> When the werewolf enters frenzy if he has marked boxes, they remain marked and after the frenzy. Using Rage for gift activation marks boxes rather than erasing them.<br /> <br /> So what do you think ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T20:14:04-07:00","id":1125770,"title":"","content":"Or you could reinstitute portions of the first edition frenzy rules, where you only needed three successes to frenzy and getting fewer successes gave you Rage points back equal to the successes that you did roll. Combined with Revised and onward making it the greater of temporary or permanent Rage to roll for frenzy, you could have a cluster of stimuli at an unfortunate time drive someone completely berserk. Just opening up the circumstances that can lead to pushing temp over perm could also work, since at the moment, it doesn't actually go over unless the ST okays it. Possibly to avoid a pretty much certainty of characters frenzying whenever they see the moon the first time at night.<br /> <br /> However, as is, i'm not sure that I buy frenzy not being dangerous enough. Especially since if you roll too many successes, you cannot stop it and you have the possibility of doing worse things than just tearing someone apart or mauling them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T01:51:04-07:00","id":1125824,"title":"","content":"Before you're every going to have good mechanics for entering Frenzy, you need fun mechanics for being in Frenzy. There's a lot of tricks in the game for avoiding Frenzy, because generally speaking, players don't want to enter Frenzy. There's no pay off to letting it happen for them. The most frequent Frenzies I see are ones after a roll to Remain Active, because that's basically the choice of Frenzy or character death; and players value their characters enough to take the Frenzy to keep them.<br /> <br /> Until you change that, changing how you enter Frenzy is either going to make the perception of Frenzy as a paper tiger worse, or make players enjoy the game less as Frenzies spend too much time playing the characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T04:20:41-07:00","id":1125839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1125716-reworking-rage-use-and-frenzy?p=1125824#post1125824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before you're every going to have good mechanics for entering Frenzy, you need fun mechanics for being in Frenzy. There's a lot of tricks in the game for avoiding Frenzy, because generally speaking, players don't want to enter Frenzy. There's no pay off to letting it happen for them. The most frequent Frenzies I see are ones after a roll to Remain Active, because that's basically the choice of Frenzy or character death; and players value their characters enough to take the Frenzy to keep them.<br /> <br /> Until you change that, changing how you enter Frenzy is either going to make the perception of Frenzy as a paper tiger worse, or make players enjoy the game less as Frenzies spend too much time playing the characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will need to playtest that first and see how it goes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T04:29:25-07:00","id":1125840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1125716-reworking-rage-use-and-frenzy?p=1125770#post1125770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or you could reinstitute portions of the first edition frenzy rules, where you only needed three successes to frenzy and getting fewer successes gave you Rage points back equal to the successes that you did roll. Combined with Revised and onward making it the greater of temporary or permanent Rage to roll for frenzy, you could have a cluster of stimuli at an unfortunate time drive someone completely berserk. Just opening up the circumstances that can lead to pushing temp over perm could also work, since at the moment, it doesn't actually go over unless the ST okays it. Possibly to avoid a pretty much certainty of characters frenzying whenever they see the moon the first time at night.<br /> <br /> However, as is, i'm not sure that I buy frenzy not being dangerous enough. Especially since if you roll too many successes, you cannot stop it and you have the possibility of doing worse things than just tearing someone apart or mauling them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I have considered about that possibility, because as it is the 3 out of 5 starting (and not only) auspicies are impossible to frenzy, and frenzy should be a considerable personal threat for every werewolf character and not only ahrouns and maybe galliards.<br /> <br /> And yes I need to find somehing about the moon issue, with the rules I am thinking it only aids frenzy and not Rage, and it should affect both.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T09:25:31-07:00","id":1126738,"title":"","content":"I think that I will keep the moon phase only as a dissadvantage and an easier way to frenzy. Rage with the current rules becomes stronger because you don't have to spend it, but decide how deep you want to dive depending on the Rage level a character has.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 08-09-2017, 12:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T10:34:34-07:00","id":1126765,"title":"","content":"You are effectively talking about infinite extra actions though if you do not have a Rage score, which is problematic. In addition, I disagree that frenzied should be fun, as you have an equal chance of going berserk or running like a rabbit (this is also true during any event that triggers the First Change). There is nothing fun about losing control, so Garou should seek to avoid frenzy as much as possible if they have a choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T11:36:28-07:00","id":1126784,"title":"","content":"No infinite Rage actions.<br /> <br /> For example, Ragabashes and Theurges have only one Rage action per turn, Philodoxes and Galliards two and Ahroun 3. Every Rage use brings you closer to frenzy, in which starting werewolves, except from ahrouns, are almost immune. Only galliards come second to ahroun and only at gibbous and full moon times (iclunding being in crinos). Frenzy immunity to the 3 out of 5 character creation population is antithematic for the horror element of werewolf.<br /> <br /> I don't do it because I find frenzy fun, but because I want to make it dangerous for all auspicies, not only ahroun and galliards under circumstances, and make players taking seriously in consideration if and when they will use Rage, now even a ragabash may enter frenzy by rolling his temporary Rage but he doesn't become very powerful with two actions per turn if he wants to take the risk of losing control. <br /> <br /> Now gifts that manipulate and control Rage and frenzy are more important, like Metis <i>Curse of Hatred</i> because it increases your chance for frenzy while decreasing your willpower, but with the normal rules it was a gift no Metis player would ever bother to buy.<br /> <br /> Of course if you have a better proposal I am more than happy to hear about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T11:42:57-07:00","id":1126787,"title":"","content":"In my games I have the players count 10s as two successes on Rage, Gnosis and Willpower rolls. Its simple, the players like it, and it hasn't caused any problems at our table. In fact, its lead to very good role-playing as the Ragabash frets about becoming the same type of raging monster as the one that ripped him a new one (the pack's Ahroun - in their first combat... ouch.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm","name":"ThomasM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T12:00:31-07:00","id":1126796,"title":"","content":"@<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> <br /> Do you know where may I find a copy of 1st edition Werewolf ?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T12:06:33-07:00","id":1126800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThomasM</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1125716-reworking-rage-use-and-frenzy?p=1126787#post1126787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my games I have the players count 10s as two successes on Rage, Gnosis and Willpower rolls. Its simple, the players like it, and it hasn't caused any problems at our table. In fact, its lead to very good role-playing as the Ragabash frets about becoming the same type of raging monster as the one that ripped him a new one (the pack's Ahroun - in their first combat... ouch.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe reroll 10's and count as 2 suxs as well? Would that be too mean ? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T13:41:05-07:00","id":1126830,"title":"","content":"Two successes per '10' on Rage rolls? Wow, that means that Thrall of the Wyrm must occur a whole lot more in your games...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T13:56:01-07:00","id":1126836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1125716-reworking-rage-use-and-frenzy?p=1126796#post1126796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\">Saur Ops Specialist</a><br /> Do you know where may I find a copy of 1st edition Werewolf ?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Used book stores for older, somewhat beaten-up and worn copies, or Drivethru RPG for an easy to find pdf. Beware: early installment weirdness abounds, and Renown comes in huge numbers on par with D&amp;D XP, and it's actually not all that different from later editions, so you won't be doing much with it if you're just trying to refurbish some of the earlier mechanics. One other notable thing, though, was that at least 1e realized that frenzies could be impactful enough without the forced symmetry of Triatic Wyrm associations and Thrall.<br /> <br /> (Drivethru can also get you something that didn't exist beforehand - a hardcover version of the first edition core, as any that were actually printed in the old days would have been softcovers. It's on the WW part of DTRPG, though, rather than the Onyx Path section.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T21:39:28-07:00","id":1126955,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11683\" data-vbnamecard=\"11683\">Aya Tari</a> <br /> <br /> When I say fun, I mean for the player, not the character.<br /> <br /> Being in a tough fight where you barely survive with 6 Agg, and you're out of WP and Rage? That's fun, because it's exciting. But that's an utter shit situation for the character.<br /> <br /> Things can be bad for your character, and still be fun for you. But it takes some work from the system to make rewarding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T21:46:50-07:00","id":1126959,"title":"","content":"I am not sure that it is fun for me as a player to have a character on death's door without any options. In fact, it usually meant that my character would miss the next few game sessions when they were that bad off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T03:22:46-07:00","id":1127032,"title":"","content":"Regardless of how much you want to twist things to justify nitpicking the example for made up things that wouldn't be fun for you personally, can you at least acknowledge and address the more general point?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T07:56:21-07:00","id":1127117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1125716-reworking-rage-use-and-frenzy?p=1126830#post1126830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two successes per '10' on Rage rolls? Wow, that means that Thrall of the Wyrm must occur a whole lot more in your games...</div> </div> </div> </div>Only once, when banes used the Incite Frenzy (or whatever its called) charm. It comes close at times, but hasn't tipped over that mark again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm","name":"ThomasM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T08:04:30-07:00","id":1127122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1125716-reworking-rage-use-and-frenzy?p=1126800#post1126800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Maybe reroll 10's and count as 2 suxs as well? Would that be too mean ? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Just a wee tad bit.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm","name":"ThomasM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T09:01:28-07:00","id":1127154,"title":"","content":"Guys I am aware that Rage is probably is getting slightly more powerful when you have higher wilpower but you are not immune to frenzy because of that, there are many powers that incite frenzy and gazing at the moon may be dangerous too, if I don't use the first time moon gazing to relieve rage boxes depending on the auspice of the character, but it would be antithematic with the reduction on frenzy difficulty. <br /> <br /> @<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm\">ThomasM</a> <br /> You gave me a touch of temptation there buddy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></b><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T09:34:17-07:00","id":1127173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1125716-reworking-rage-use-and-frenzy?p=1126959#post1126959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not sure that it is fun for me as a player to have a character on <b>death's door</b> without any options. In fact, it usually meant that my character would miss the next few game sessions when they were that bad off.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;More dust. More ashes. More disappointment.&quot;<br /> <br /> Perhaps as a variant of Rage recovery, you could have characters on the verge of being incapacitated/killed roll Rage to remain conscious (and alive, in the case of lethal and agg)...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T10:45:57-07:00","id":1127194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1125716-reworking-rage-use-and-frenzy?p=1127173#post1127173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps as a variant of Rage recovery, you could have characters on the verge of being incapacitated/killed roll Rage to remain conscious (and alive, in the case of lethal and agg)...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You may opt to modify the Rage roll to remain active to a difficulty appropriate to the moon phase, diff 8 for new moon, 7 for crescent moon etc etc. Guys (not you <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Saur Ops Specialist) solutions exist. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T11:34:38-07:00","id":1127218,"title":"","content":"I do not really see the existing Rage rolls as a problem that needs a solution. Garou without high Rage are less combat capable than Garou with high Rage, but they suffer less of the negative effects of Rage. And temporary Rage can exceed permanent Rage (unlike temporary Gnosis or temporary Willpower), which becomes a problem when Garou see the moon for the first time during a night because Rage rolls default to temporary Rage if temporary Rage exceeds permanent Rage (as they gain a set amount of temporary Rage unless the moon is in their auspice). A Ragabash with permanent Rage 1 who perceives the full moon will go to five points of temporary Rage until they can work through the excess temporary Rage, which means that they can go into frenzy quite easily. An Ahroun with permanent Rage 5 in the same circumstance is not particularly disadvantaged because she refills her Rage up to her permanent Rage (and she can burn Rage much more quickly than a Ragabash with permanent Rage 1).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T12:21:37-07:00","id":1127239,"title":"","content":"Yes but Ragabashes don't gain that high Rage often, extremely rarely in a campaign or in moot sessions which always take place in full moon nights.<br /> Which means that in the majority of a campaign a player may consider he is frenzy free because of low Rage score. Not to mention that if a stressful situation occurs the play of a Ragabash is such that he may avoid relatively easy frenzy situations, the same happens for theurges, and more easily for philodoxes since they can burn 2 Rage in a turn for actions, that doesn't mean they cannot burn more Rage fo other reasons. The only way to make full moon dangerous for low rage auspicies is when they already have 5 rage for looking up to the full moon and they gain one more because of combat or other stressful situation. <br /> And again Rage will be dangerous for mostly one or 2 rolls, since even a ragabash may spend more rage to ignore wound penalties,resist stun or whatever you allow Rage being used for.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if you mark Rage instead of erasing, you gain closer and closer towards frenzy, you can always opt not to spend Rage of course. In my mind Rage is something that grows the more you use it not settles down, maybe after a stressful situation you may roll willpower difficulty of permanent Rage rating and erase marked boxes. <br /> ;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T13:33:33-07:00","id":1127288,"title":"","content":"But the point of Rage is that it is a limited resource (at least as far as W20 is concerned). Fera have to conserve Rage because it can mean the difference between life and death. While a character might gain a point of Rage before the beginning of conflict, while being humiliated, or when they botch a critical roll, they are only guaranteed Rage recovery when they see the moon for the first time during a night.<br /> <br /> If Rage stops being a limited resource, then characters will just keep accumulating Rage during a conflict until they frenzy, and they will keep accumulating Rage during the frenzy. There is no real reason not to accumulate Rage since the only penalty is frenzy, especially when characters are probably within a combat situation when characters are accumulating Rage. This is especially true if the character can just go meditate away the Rage. It also gets rid of many of the combat differences between auspices, as the only difference comes down to how much Rage can characters burn for extra actions, especially since a Ragabash accumulating one point of Rage per turn for 10 turns pretty much has the same effect as an Ahroun accumulating two points of Rage per turn for 5 turns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T14:15:56-07:00","id":1127322,"title":"","content":"I think the biggest design reason to adjust how Frenzy checks work, is because rolling to fail works poorly in the system. And that's how Frenzies work: you roll Rage and hope you fail. The system works considerably better if the players roll to succeed.<br /> <br /> So, a house rule that I've used to success that addresses some of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12906_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12906\" data-vbnamecard=\"12906\">Story Letter</a>'s concerns (long before V5's Hunger mechanics):<br /> <br /> Resisting Frenzy is a Willpower roll with a difficulty equal to half of the characters Rage - higher of temp or perm as usual - rounded up, plus 0 to 4 based on moon phase, plus 1 if it's your moon. Failure is a normal Frenzy, botch is Thrall, you can't spend WP on the roll it self.<br /> <br /> This means even a Ragabash on a new moon could still fail their roll (if rarely since it's a diff 2 roll at Rage 1). And Ahrouns aren't quite as boned as they are in the current rules if they're keeping their WP equal to the Rage to avoid the penalties for not doing so. At Rage 5 on a full moon the base difficulty for an Ahroun is 8, so with WP 5 they're at around 64% to pass a Frenzy check. Which is actually pretty close to their current risk odds, but Ahroun players can invest in more WP too.<br /> <br /> This also slots easily into the existing mechanics. Rank bonuses that increase the difficulty on Frenzy checks now decrease it by the same amount, etc. Rage rolls still risk Frenzy as well, but that is something purposefully built into anything that rolls Rage as a dice-pool as part of a risk-reward for the power it offers (Remaining Active, using Rage to replace Intimidation, etc.).<br /> <br /> While I agree that letting characters have unlimited access to Rage as long as they're willing to risk the Frenzy isn't a great move (unless you want to completely redo a lot of other things), I do disagree that low Rage characters aren't dangerous combatants. They just use different tactics than the furry blender default. Low Rage - and esp. higher Gnosis - characters are much better suited towards using active Fetishes and Talens in battle (activating them is Gnosis based compared to relying on the passive benefits of something like a klaive). A well built grappling werewolf (though the idea that Hispo and Lupus forms can't initiate grapples is always kinda weird to me), doesn't really benefit as much from Rage actions, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T14:36:24-07:00","id":1127334,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> yeah when one makes a change in a rule must be prepared to change other things as well.<br /> Your willpower idea is not bad, it helps alot, but there is still the mood problem, yes I agree that low Rage auspicies have their own ways of dealing with danger, but I have never seen these same auspicies be afraid of frenzy, they where always like klein mein, let ahrouns deal with that problem, the ahroun deal with the issue by increasing willpower and voila, frenzy danger becomes spoofed. The willpower idea of yours indeed keeps the dangerous part of Rage.<br /> <br /> By the way hispo and lupus can grapple with their jaws, jaw lock etc. etc. It's just not like homid like, it takes greater effort to pin down an enemy but when you do its far more deadly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 08-10-2017, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T17:01:29-07:00","id":1127403,"title":"","content":"Another possible problem with having unlimited Rage is that Garou never lose the wolf and always have the ability to recover from stun or remain active. That makes Garou even more powerful combat monsters, as they always have a chance of coming back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T04:23:18-07:00","id":1127559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1125716-reworking-rage-use-and-frenzy?p=1127403#post1127403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another possible problem with having unlimited Rage is that Garou never lose the wolf and always have the ability to recover from stun or remain active. That makes Garou even more powerful combat monsters, as they always have a chance of coming back.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yup this is indeed a problem that needs tobe solved, I would rule that if you spend all your willpower you automatically lose the wolf and you erase all your Rage boxes.<br /> Any proposals ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T13:14:59-07:00","id":1127752,"title":"","content":"How much of a change are you willing to make to the rest of the rules? Radically changing how Rage works means rewriting a lot of stuff, and at a certain point there needs to be a decision to just reconsider all of it as a whole and build it up from there, or experiment with patching things over repeatedly to make the change work.<br /> <br /> The &quot;spend all your WP&quot; thing has a tendency to work very poorly (mostly from past community discussions on making running low/out of WP a bit more meaningful) because it just means people don't spend that last point of WP unless they're forced to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T01:31:13-07:00","id":1127973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1125716-reworking-rage-use-and-frenzy?p=1127752#post1127752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much of a change are you willing to make to the rest of the rules? Radically changing how Rage works means rewriting a lot of stuff, and at a certain point there needs to be a decision to just reconsider all of it as a whole and build it up from there, or experiment with patching things over repeatedly to make the change work.<br /> <br /> The &quot;spend all your WP&quot; thing has a tendency to work very poorly (mostly from past community discussions on making running low/out of WP a bit more meaningful) because it just means people don't spend that last point of WP unless they're forced to.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is ultimately true !<br /> And indeed I am planning on changing what is needed to be changed.<br /> <br /> In <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">order</span></span></span> to help you, I will tell you how I ran Rage and what effects it had on the other elements.<br /> <br /> Because we ran huge and long non stop sessions, which could easily count as multiple chronicles, but it was indeed one large chronicle that lasted an entire year, broken mostly in 3 parts.<br /> Characters had many options to replenish Rage, Gnosis and willpower, since a 9-12 hours session real life could be from on day to a week in game. Players learned to control Rage in such manner that it was extremely rare to enter frenzy but quite easy to keep temporary Rage in aidful levels, our philodox had rage 5 with extremely high willpower the ahroun had equal rage and willpower etc etc. Of course they increased their stats with the appropriate role playing, but given their higher rank status things became even easier for frenzy checks.<br /> So even though Rage in a combat was easy to be maintained, the players often claimed that even Rage 10 is not enough, because the more you have the more you burn, maybe the reason was that I allowed Rage expediture for automatic succs on physical actions and damage-soak or to forfeit stamina roll for regeneration. So players had more options and thus Rage evaporated even faster. On the other hand I only had 2 frenzies because of Rage rolls and they both happened in the same session, one was thrall of wyrm too, but guys 2 frenzies in a 3,5 year old campaign is a realy bad rate.<br /> <br /> More often was the Curse effect than frenzy, yes we had many frenzies because of Remainig active rolls but only two from normal frenzy rolls, and that happened because of good Rage management, ok being a smart werewolf is <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">worty for</span></span></span> Renown awarding but I don't think the developers had that in mind when creating Rage mechanics.<br /> Not to mention that no player ever lost the wolf, because the most times a werewolf was about to use his last willpower it was for a realy desperate reason, and when he succeeded it was so awesome that he actually gained it back, that of course happened extremely rarely as well.<br /> <br /> In parallel with our Apocalypse campaing we where running a crossover WoD and in our party we had a werewolf whose frenzy was a major issue, he entered frenzy in avery session and he killed or decimated at least 3 player characters. That made me think that THIS is the real frenzy that makes people have nightamares for werewolves, though I prefered frenzy to be some kind of a danger rather than a great possibility to happen and victimize player characters.<br /> <br /> So I am trying to find a way to make Rage an element that poots a player deeper to the monstrosity a werewolf is, to thrill and terrify the player, not to make Rage just one more game element.<br /> The greatest issue is that creating mood-wise rules sometimes come against playwise rules. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11683\" data-vbnamecard=\"11683\">Aya Tari</a> mentioned above, what will I do about the moon phase rage replenishing, or with losing the wolf. All these are considerable issues, so far the changes I made aid some Rage related Gifts, but indeed leave behind some system mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 08-12-2017, 04:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T05:06:22-07:00","id":1128009,"title":"","content":"I am curious why people are acting like every frenzy is a berserk frenzy. Among Garou, frenzies should be equally likely to be berserk or fox frenzies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T08:16:34-07:00","id":1128050,"title":"","content":"In the books there is no system on how to choose berserk or fox frenzy, there may be an errata somewhere I don't know. In my humble opinion, fox frenzy should kick in when your character faces an impossibly horrifying threat like a nexus crawler or when he enters frenzy after taking a wound that brings him to cripple and he is close to death, or maybe a botched frenzy roll, if the story teller allows botches on Rage rolls. Or by failing a willpower roll check for courage.<br /> The rate of berserk or fox frenzies depends highly on the style of the session.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T09:49:56-07:00","id":1128078,"title":"","content":"I just flip a coin because most events that could cause berserk frenzy should also be capable of causing fox frenzy. In either case, the character potentially breaks the Veil though, so they may have problems if there are mortal witnesses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T11:02:33-07:00","id":1128088,"title":"","content":"I would recomment to check the reason of frenzy, it it happened bcause of hate then its aberserk one, if it happened because of fear then its a fox one. A coin is rather mean, but if it works for your party and you have fun fine by me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T19:10:01-07:00","id":1128299,"title":"","content":"The thought occurs that if you worked frenzies as being resisted instead of a nitroglycerine sensitivity roll, you could give two different resistance ratings, one for either type of frenzy, and then differentiate tribes and such based on which frenzies they were better at resisting, like how Orpheus has bits of its Temper traits divided among various splat choices. For auspices, there could be a sliding scale of dice for frenzy resistance where Ragabash gets the most to resist going berserk and Ahroun gains the most to resist the fox, for example, while being Homid might give a greater bonus to resist going berserk with little resistance to fox frenzies, while Lupus has middling additions to both and Metis has substantial increases to both, because that comes with the territory of being locked in your ragemonster form for 8-10 years.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1125716-reworking-rage-use-and-frenzy?p=1128050#post1128050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the books there is no system on how to choose berserk or fox frenzy, there may be an errata somewhere I don't know. In my humble opinion, fox frenzy should kick in when your character faces an impossibly horrifying threat like a nexus crawler or when he enters frenzy after taking a wound that brings him to cripple and he is close to death, or maybe a botched frenzy roll, if the story teller allows botches on Rage rolls. Or by failing a willpower roll check for courage.<br /> The rate of berserk or fox frenzies depends highly on the style of the session.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've heard that there are clearer guidelines in DA: Werewolf about when either one is what you're rolling for, but I don't have the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T19:15:34-07:00","id":1128303,"title":"","content":"In the game I played and the one I ran, we just let people choose whether it was Berserk or Fox. I feel like players should have a good idea of what makes sense in the circumstances.<br /> <br /> As far as Rage rolls, my group always used 10's counting twice for Frenzy. I'm actually not a fan of it. As someone else pointed out, it makes Thrall of the Wyrm much more likely. At even 4 Rage, if you play long enough, people WILL Thrall. And 5-6 Rage becomes almost unplayable. I actually think it's okay for 3 Rage and under being un-Frenziable. If someone is deciding to stay that low on Rage, their combat effectiveness drops considerably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7550-vulcan7200","name":"Vulcan7200","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T04:10:05-07:00","id":1128383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1125716-reworking-rage-use-and-frenzy?p=1128299#post1128299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've heard that there are clearer guidelines in DA: Werewolf about when either one is what you're rolling for, but I don't have the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>The revised DA Werewolf actually backs up my opinion, it also adds that battle and anger brings forth berserk frenzy, while horror encounter brings forth fox frenzy.<br /> <br /> I can only further it with a house rule that when a werewolf faces something terrifying, be it a bane, a monstrous fomor or another werewolf, to compare his Rage or willpower to the Rage of the horriffic encounter when checking for frenzy, if the roll succeeds (with original rules), and bring 4 successes and the horror has greater Rage than the werewolf's trait then the werewolf enters fox frenzy, if the werewolf has greater Rage or willpower, story teller's choice, the werewolf enters berserk frenzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 11-22-2017, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}